 decision('local:catalog:mechanical-stress',['Q13409892'],'quarantine_central_decision','The current force-per-area/loading-mode takeaway overlaps the stress state represented by the registered Cauchy stress tensor. Different stress measures can support a broader topic, but an introductory versus tensor presentation alone is not a sufficient new learning identity. Central coordinator instructed quarantine of this proposal and replacement from a separately supported reserve.', ['source-cache/e02.json passages 6–8; baseline-index concepts/Q13409892','https://www.sandia.gov/files/sierra/SM_Theory_5_18/main/stress_measures.html §7.1 and §7.3'],['Do not relabel this introductory explanation as a novel fine subject. Preserve the proposal and the baseline ID.']),
 decision('local:catalog:three-point-bending-test',['Q7202074','local:catalog:research-batch-001:springback-in-sheet-metal-bending'],'admit_replacement_recommended','The test uses a simply supported specimen and a central point load to infer elastic stiffness from deflection. Plastic bending concerns irreversible bending response; springback concerns recovery after unloading a forming process. The test configuration is a distinct application, also distinct from Young’s modulus or the neutral-axis concept alone.',['source-cache/e42.json passages 215–217, paragraphs 216–218'],['Use the ideal elastic, small-deflection beam-model conditions for the displayed stiffness relation.']),
