 decision('local:catalog:torque-induced-gyroscopic-precession',['Q104225'],'admit_qualified_facet_central_decision','General precession is axis-direction change. This source-supported subset is the torque-driven, fast-spinning gyroscope case in which torque perpendicular to angular momentum changes its direction. It is not a second unrestricted Precession identity.',['source-cache/p04.json passages 6, 7, 17'],['Explicitly retain torque-induced scope and fast-spin/slow-precession condition: precession angular velocity much less than the disk spin angular velocity. Do not imply gyroscopic precession is always torque-driven.']),
 decision('local:catalog:pitch-material',['Q167510','Q1103750'],'admit_with_sense_boundary','The UQ source identifies the selected pitch as a derivative of tar and demonstrates brittle short-time behavior and very slow flow. Baseline Asphalt is described as a petroleum material; Concert pitch is a musical reference frequency. The intended tar-derived material is distinct, but generic pitch terminology can overlap bitumen/asphalt, so the material sense must be explicit.',['source-cache/c19.json passages 4, 6, 8, 9, 11; baseline-index concepts/Q167510 and Q1103750'],['Add Asphalt Q167510 to the actual meaning comparisons and specify tar-derived pitch in the takeaway/card. Do not use the musical homonym alone as evidence of novelty.']),
 decision('local:catalog:graph-laplacian',['Q451881'],'retain_quarantine','A graph Laplacian is a standard discrete Laplace operator on a graph. A different label or a degree-minus-adjacency formula does not by itself establish an identity beyond the registered operator. This is outside the recommended 200.',['selection.proposed.json issue b004-i01; baseline-index concepts/Q451881']),
 decision('local:catalog:homeomorphism',['Q584521'],'admit_distinct_scope','General topological homeomorphism is a continuous bijection with a continuous inverse. The registered graph-theoretic relation is graph equivalence by subdivisions; this does not absorb the general mapping concept.',['selection.proposed.json proposal 66; baseline-index concepts/Q584521']),
 decision('local:catalog:eulers-polyhedron-formula',['Q852973','Q184871'],'admit_qualified_facet','Euler’s polyhedron formula is the sphere-like polyhedral case V−E+F=2 of the broader Euler-characteristic invariant, not the complex-exponential Euler formula. The significant nearest baseline is Q852973 as well as the homonymous Q184871.',['selection.proposed.json proposals 52 and 77; baseline-index concepts/Q852973 and Q184871'],['Keep the sphere-like/genus-zero condition and explain the special-case relation to Euler characteristic; do not present another unrestricted Euler-characteristic identity.']),
 decision('local:catalog:memoryless-property',['Q176645'],'admit_distinct_property','Waiting-time memorylessness is invariance of the residual-wait distribution after elapsed waiting; the Markov property conditions future evolution on current state. These are related but different claims and the new distributional scope is explicit.',['selection.proposed.json proposal 89; baseline-index concepts/Q176645']),
 decision('local:catalog:conditional-expectation',['Q200125'],'admit_distinct_property','Conditioning preserves specified information and produces an information-dependent random variable; an unconditional expected value averages over that uncertainty.',['selection.proposed.json proposal 92; baseline-index concepts/Q200125']),
 decision('local:catalog:critical-point-of-a-fluid',['local:catalog:supercritical-fluid'],'admit_distinct_boundary','The critical point is the endpoint of the liquid-vapor coexistence curve. A supercritical fluid is the region/state beyond the critical temperature and pressure. Boundary and region are separate supported learning subjects.',['selection.proposed.json proposal 32; baseline-index concepts/local:catalog:supercritical-fluid']),
